Z||000000||JohnnyK||01-16-2001||07:18 PM||||As I was trying to figure out my horn problem (didn't work) I went trouble shooting. Whenever I pressed the horn, there was this clicking from the "Convenience center" and I think it was coming from this white box right above the flasher. So I took it out, and the clicking stopped. Before I decided to look for another one of those, I figured out that the problem was a bad connection on the actual horn, but my question is what is that white box? A horn relay or something? Thanks (Also, is the headlight relay on the driver side or passenger side?)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Indiana_resto_guy||01-16-2001||08:21 PM||||It's called a 'horn relay' and MUST be in place for the horn to operate.<BR>If the horn still doesn't work check for 12 volts at the plug with button depressed and relay in place. If you have 12 volts, buy a new horn.||||reg||1
